{"id":"s4.5.4","slug":"repeating-decimals-in-other-bases-same-base","title":"Repeating Decimals in Other Bases - Keeping Same Base","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">To convert a repeating decimal in base $b$ to a fraction in the same base, you can first convert to a base-10 fraction and then convert the numerator and denominator back to base $b$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For example, to convert $0.444..._8$ to a base-8 fraction: First, convert to base 10: $\\frac{4}{7}$. Then convert the numerator and denominator to base 8: $4_{10}=4_8$ and $7_{10}=7_8$. So the answer is $\\frac{4_8}{7_8}$.</p>","summary":"To convert a repeating decimal in base to a fraction in the same base, you can first convert to a base-10 fraction and then convert the numerator and denominator back to base .","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem converting a repeating decimal in base-b to a fraction in base-b.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Change $0.111..._3$ to a base-3 fraction.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":2,"text":"Change $0.222..._4$ to a base-4 fraction.","answer":"2/3","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":3,"text":"Change $0.333..._5$ to a base-5 fraction.","answer":"3/4","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":4,"text":"Change $0.444..._6$ to a base-6 fraction.","answer":"4/5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":5,"text":"Change $0.555..._7$ to a base-7 fraction.","answer":"5/6","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":6,"text":"Change $0.666..._8$ to a base-8 fraction.","answer":"6/7","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":7,"text":"Change $0.777..._9$ to a base-9 fraction.","answer":"7/8","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bases","repeating-decimals"]},{"id":8,"text":"Change $0.222..._5$ to a base-5 fraction.","answer":"2/4","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","bas